### excluded branch: agency food product type  (6074 classes)
#   parallel regulatory classification vocabularies (EFSA FoodEx2, US CFR, EC,
#   CCPR). '00030 - cereal grains' alone groups wheat, maize, rye, barley and
#   rice, so traversing this branch leaks corn into wheat without ever
#   ascending the food hierarchy. See audit F10.
obo:FOODON_03400361 local:excludedFromTraversal true .
### excluded branch: embryo  (12 classes)
#   UBERON developmental stages -- morula, blastula, gastrula, neurula,
#   2/4/8-cell stage. FoodOn parents `embryo` under `animal egg`, which is
#   defensible biologically: an egg does contain one. But these are stages of
#   development, not things that appear on a plate or a label, and they are
#   the only non-food members of the animal egg subtree. Excluded when `animal
#   egg` was added as a root for the `egg` query, so that adding quail, goose
#   and ostrich egg did not also add 12 embryology classes. Whole branch is
#   UBERON and 12 classes; no food class sits under it.
obo:UBERON_0000922 local:excludedFromTraversal true .

# --- parallel-hierarchy correspondences -------------------------------------
